[Music]  so we started talking to the mayor of  bandung in 2016 when he wanted to make  bandung a more livable city a more happy  city and increase the happiness index of  its citizens so he first got in contact  with him  through one of his partners the guy who  was leading the smart city initiative of  bendung  so we began talking and really had a lot  of discussion of how we can include the  citizens into creating new innovations  into getting involved in  making the city more livable  so we decided to go for a crowdsourcing  contest because indonesia is really an  interesting market in this regard they  are really keen on using social media  and these kind of platforms to  communicate so i think around that time  jakarta  was  announced to be the number one tweeting  city in the world so really the social  media usage in this country was really  high so it was a great way to connect  different people and to collect a lot of  different ideas and problems on an  online platform so really this kind of  pre-existing conditions in the community  allowed us to  use this method and we really wanted to  understand what moved these people what  were the problems that they had so  that's why we decided to really go for  finding problems finding out what the  needs of the people were what kind of  ideas they already had to solve them  really to get a better understanding of  the community of the people of what was  the issue at the core of the city of  bandung we didn't really have a lot of  expectations this was kind of the first  initiative regarding crowdsourcing in  indonesia we hope to get a lot of  submissions  because the mayor of bandung really has  a lot of  reach in the region so he is  what in asia is called the key opinion  leader what we may call in the western  world an influencer so he has a lot of  twitter followers who we expected to  reach a lot of people  but we never expected to really get so  many people to participate to join the  discussion to submit their problems to  submit their ideas and to contribute to  this contest so we were very kind of  overwhelmed of how well this kind of  initiative worked in indonesia  throughout the contest we collected more  than 1600 ideas and from all different  kind of topics from  transportation healthcare environment  education so the people really submitted  a lot of their problems that they had  and solutions that they would like to  see implemented overall more than 5000  people registered on the platform so  really a big amount of the  citizens really got engaged here and  actually took the step of taking part  actively not just reading about it not  just listening to what the mayor had to  say there were about 16 000  people visiting the platform during the  time of the of the contest but 5000  people actually actually signed up and  actively engaged with the community

